  "caption": "Quinn has been starting the gym \"next Monday\" since March, while sitting for nine hours a day.\n\nGood news: short bouts count. Exercise snacks of one or two minutes, spread through the day, can add up, and sitting breaks help too.\n\nEasy ideas: take the stairs at a brisk pace, do calf raises while brushing your teeth, fit in sit-to-stands between meetings, and get up every 30 to 45 minutes. If you already train, snacks are a bonus rather than a swap.\n\nIf you have a heart condition or have been inactive for a long time, check with your GP before adding vigorous bursts. If joint pain limits stairs or squats, a physio can help you find options that suit you.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
